From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] zygote: read os.version again in each specialized process

libcore sets os.version once from uname(), in
initUnchangeableSystemProperties(). Zygote runs as root, so with
patches/kernel/core/0008 it gets the real release and every app
inherits it, while uname() in the same app returns the release the
kernel reports to it.

callPostForkChildHooks() runs after setresuid() in SpecializeCommon(),
for system_server, apps, USAPs and child zygotes, so reading uname()
there gives each process the release the kernel reports to it. Nothing
changes for system_server. setUnchangeableSystemProperty() is hidden
outside the core platform API, hence the reflection. With ART's
hiddenapi_platform_enforcement flag enabled the call fails and logs a
warning; the cp2a release configuration leaves it off.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [goes with patches/kernel/core/0008]
---
 core/java/com/android/internal/os/Zygote.java | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/core/java/com/android/internal/os/Zygote.java b/core/java/com/android/internal/os/Zygote.java
index 5a2f526..62005da 100644
--- a/core/java/com/android/internal/os/Zygote.java
+++ b/core/java/com/android/internal/os/Zygote.java
@@ -1182,6 +1182,14 @@ public final class Zygote {
     private static void callPostForkChildHooks(int runtimeFlags, boolean isSystemServer,
             boolean isZygote, String instructionSet) {
         ZygoteHooks.postForkChild(runtimeFlags, isSystemServer, isZygote, instructionSet);
+        // Zygote read os.version as root, and the kernel may report another release to
+        // apps. The uid is final here, so read it again.
+        try {
+            System.class.getMethod("setUnchangeableSystemProperty", String.class, String.class)
+                    .invoke(null, "os.version", Os.uname().release);
+        } catch (ReflectiveOperationException e) {
+            Log.w("Zygote", "Could not refresh os.version", e);
+        }
     }
 
     /**
